# Local insecure CockroachDB clusters

Every CockroachDB node and cluster this project starts must run **locally** in **Docker or Podman**. Detect the engine (Docker vs Podman) the same way as the Engineering Tool; do not start `cockroach` on the host, on Cloud, Kubernetes, or roachprod.

Every node must use **`--insecure`**. SQL clients use `--insecure` / `sslMode: disable`. Do not add cert volumes, secure compose files, CertManager, or a secure-mode toggle.

```text
# BAD — host binary, TLS, or remote
cockroach start --certs-dir=./certs --advertise-addr=my.cloud.host

# GOOD — local engine, insecure
podman/docker run ... cockroach start --insecure --locality=region=eu-west,zone=eu-west-1
```

Publish SQL and DB Console only on localhost (HAProxy). Do not introduce Cloud, Kubernetes, or remote-cluster paths unless the user explicitly overrides this rule.
